---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import '~/styles/legal.css';

export const prerender = true;

const UPDATED = '5 August 2026';
const DISCORD = 'https://discord.com/invite/2sYR5YdRpH';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The rules for using PoGo TXK — a volunteer-run community site for Pokémon GO players in Texarkana, Texas and Arkansas."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <p class="legal-eyebrow">PoGo TXK</p>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="legal-summary">
      <p><strong>The short version.</strong></p>
      <p>
        Be decent to other trainers. Play safely and legally — obey park hours, watch the road,
        and never trespass. Do not cheat at Pokémon GO or ask us to help you cheat.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is a free, volunteer-run fan site with no guarantees. We can remove content or
        accounts that cause problems for the community.
      </p>
    </div>

    <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Contents">
      <p>Contents</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#agreement">The agreement</a></li>
        <li><a href="#who">Who can use this</a></li>
        <li><a href="#conduct">How to behave</a></li>
        <li><a href="#safety">Safety and the real world</a></li>
        <li><a href="#cheating">Cheating</a></li>
        <li><a href="#content">Content you post</a></li>
        <li><a href="#accuracy">Accuracy of the map</a></li>
        <li><a href="#moderation">Moderation</a></li>
        <li><a href="#ip">Intellectual property</a></li>
        <li><a href="#warranty">No warranty</a></li>
        <li><a href="#liability">Liability</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="agreement">1. The agreement</h2>
    <p>
      By using PoGo TXK you agree to these terms. If you do not, please do not use the site.
      PoGo TXK is a volunteer-run community project, not a company, and the site is provided
      free of charge.
    </p>

    <h2 id="who">2. Who can use this</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone may read the site. Signing in requires a Discord account, so Discord's own minimum
      age applies — at least 13, and higher in some countries. Some features are limited to
      members of the PoGo TXK Discord server.
    </p>

    <h2 id="conduct">3. How to behave</h2>
    <p>Our <a href="/conduct">Code of Conduct</a> applies everywhere, including here. In short, do not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Harass, threaten, demean or bully anyone</li>
      <li>Post hateful content targeting anyone's race, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability or nationality</li>
      <li>Share anyone's personal information without their consent — including a home address, workplace, or real name they have not chosen to share</li>
      <li>Post sexual content, gore, or anything illegal</li>
      <li>Spam, advertise, or promote account-selling and other services that violate Niantic's terms</li>
      <li>Impersonate other trainers, ambassadors, or Niantic staff</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="safety">4. Safety and the real world</h2>
    <p>
      This site shows real, physical locations and encourages people to walk to them. That
      carries real-world risk, and we need to be direct about it:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Watch where you are going.</strong> Do not play while driving, cycling, or crossing roads.</li>
      <li><strong>Respect the park.</strong> Obey posted hours, signage, and staff instructions. Do not enter closed or restricted areas.</li>
      <li><strong>Do not trespass.</strong> A location appearing on our map is not permission to enter private property.</li>
      <li><strong>Be aware of your surroundings</strong>, particularly after dark. Consider going with others.</li>
      <li><strong>Under-18s should have a parent or guardian's permission</strong> before attending a meetup.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Meetups are informal gatherings of community members, not supervised or insured events.
      You attend at your own risk and remain responsible for yourself and for any children in
      your care.
    </p>

    <h2 id="cheating">5. Cheating</h2>
    <p>
      We do not support cheating in Pokémon GO, and you may not use this site to organise or
      promote it. That includes GPS spoofing, multi-accounting, bots, modified clients, and
      account sharing or selling.
    </p>
    <p>
      Any companion app we publish never interacts with Pokémon GO. It does not read your
      screen, hook into the game, or alter your location — it only talks to this site and our
      own Discord server. If you find something claiming to be ours that does otherwise, it is
      not ours, and you should tell us.
    </p>

    <h2 id="content">6. Content you post</h2>
    <p>
      You keep ownership of photos, descriptions and messages you contribute. By posting them
      you give PoGo TXK permission to display them on this site and on our community channels.
      You can ask us to remove your content at any time.
    </p>
    <p>Only post content you have the right to post. In particular:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not upload photographs you did not take unless you have permission and can credit the photographer.</li>
      <li>If people are identifiable in a photo, be considerate — remove it on request.</li>
      <li>Press photographs on this site remain the property of their publications and are used with credit.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="accuracy">7. Accuracy of the map</h2>
    <p>
      Location data is maintained by volunteers and reflects the game as we last observed it.
      PokéStops and Gyms are added, moved and removed by Niantic without notice. Event and raid
      information comes from third-party sources and may be wrong or out of date.
    </p>
    <p>
      Treat everything here as a helpful guess, not an authority. Do not rely on it for
      navigation or for anything that matters.
    </p>

    <h2 id="moderation">8. Moderation</h2>
    <p>
      Ambassadors and admins may edit or remove content, and suspend or ban accounts, where
      that protects the community. We aim to be fair and to explain ourselves, but this is a
      volunteer project — we cannot promise a formal appeals process. Serious disputes are
      handled in the Discord server.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ip">9. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Pokémon and Pokémon character names are trademarks of Nintendo. Pokémon GO is a trademark
      of Niantic, Inc. PoGo TXK is an unofficial fan community and is not affiliated with,
      endorsed by, or sponsored by Niantic, Nintendo, Creatures Inc., GAME FREAK, or The Pokémon
      Company. Game-related imagery and names are used for identification under what we believe
      is fair use, and remain the property of their owners.
    </p>
    <p>
      Map data is © OpenStreetMap contributors and © CARTO. Event, raid and research data comes
      from <a href="https://leekduck.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Leek Duck</a>
      via <a href="https://github.com/bigfoott/ScrapedDuck" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">ScrapedDuck</a>,
      and is used under their terms: this site carries no advertising and is free to use.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you own rights to something here and want it removed, contact us on Discord and we
      will take it down promptly.
    </p>

    <h2 id="warranty">10. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided "as is", with no warranties of any kind. We do not promise it will
      be available, accurate, complete, or free of errors. We may change or discontinue any
      part of it at any time.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">11. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, the volunteers who run PoGo TXK are not liable
      for any loss, injury or damage arising from your use of this site, from attending a
      meetup, or from travelling to any location shown on the map. You are responsible for your
      own safety and for your own account standing in Pokémon GO.
    </p>
    <p>Nothing here limits liability where the law does not allow it to be limited.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">12. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. Material changes will be announced in the Discord server and
      the date at the top will change. Continuing to use the site means you accept the update.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">13. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Reach us in the{' '}
      <a href={DISCORD} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">PoGo TXK Discord server</a> —
      message any ambassador or admin.
    </p>

    <p class="legal-note">
      See also our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and{' '}
      <a href="/conduct">Code of Conduct</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
